Modifications to the original distribution 

1. The left and right extent of character 3010 in original data were set to
   JJ.  Modified to JY.  Rick had them in his data set as JZ.  I just chose
   to use same as Rick assuming he found the correction.

/* Original line
 3010 45JZSFSWRZQ[ RTGTWSZ RUFUWTZQ[O[MZLXLVMUNUOVOWNXMX RMVMWNWNVMV RPF
XF RQFSG RRFSH RVFUH RWFUG

/* Modified line
 3010 45JZSFSWRZQ[ RTGTWSZ RUFUWTZQ[O[MZLXLVMUNUOVOWNXMX RMVMWNWNVMV RPF
XF RQFSG RRFSH RVFUH RWFUG

/* Ricks NBS data set
 3010  : -8   8:  1 -12:  1   5:  0   8: -1   9:-64   0:  2 -11:  2   5:  1   8:-64   0:  3 -12:  3   5:  2   8: -1   9: -3   9:
       : -5   8: -6   6: -6   4: -5   3: -4   3: -3   4: -3   5: -4   6: -5   6:-64   0: -5   4: -5   5: -4   5: -4   4: -5   4:
       :-64   0: -2 -12:  6 -12:-64   0: -1 -12:  1 -11:-64   0:  0 -12:  1 -10:-64   0:  4 -12:  3 -10:-64   0:  5 -12:  3 -11:
       :-64 -64:

2. The UNIX net set has defined character 997, 998 and 999.  These are two
   stroke characters appearing to be horizontal lines at various Y positions.
